CORE
gated_clock1.sv
--bound 6
^\[main\.p_hold\] always \(!main\.en \|=> \$stable\(main\.q\)\): PROVED up to bound 6$
^\[main\.p_follow\] always \(main\.en \|=> main\.q == \$past\(main\.d\)\): PROVED up to bound 6$
^\[main\.p_r\] always \(##1 main\.r == \$past\(main\.d\)\): PROVED up to bound 6$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A register on a gated clock, clk & en, only changes when en is set at the
clock edge. The base clock clk is identified by the always construct
that uses it without gating.
